> I got some resistances, though I may have been foolish in
> doing so.  Can I die from eating bees?

Potentially.  (Is there anything in NetHack that *can't*
kill you?)  It can also save your life though.

Eating one bee has a 30% (killer) or 60% (queen) chance of
granting poison resistance, but of course the corpse is
poisonous to eat, which is probably why you asked.

Eating a poisonous corpse causes a few points of damage, but
for a post-Sokoban player on the way back up from deep in
the mines, this is unlikely to cause death unless you are
already seriously injured.

The other issue to consider is the strength loss.  Eating a
small number of bee corpses in an attempt to gain poison
resistance can, if things don't go your way, put you into a
situation where attempting to carry all the armor and food
and other things you need to save your life will make you
burdened.  How many failed bee-eating endeavors are required
to put you into a dire situation will depend somewhat on
role.  Valkyries are generally going to be able to get away
with eating more bees than Tourists or Wizards.

If you happen to find an apron (or an identified ring of
poison resistance), it is worthwhile to make a point of
eating bee (and other poisonous but resistance-granting)
corpses while wearing it.  Once you get the intrinsic, you
can stash the extrinsic-granting item.

If you have a unicorn horn, I think you may be able to
recover lost strength that way.

Otherwise, you're playing odds that you'll get the intrinsic
before the strength loss becomes a serious problem.

It's better to eat blobs, puddings, cross-aligned unicorns,
flesh golems, shriekers, and so on, if you can get them.

However, if the RNG is being stingy with those monsters and
giving you lots of bees, it may be safer to eat some of the
bees (especially queen bees) than not.  Not having the
resistance for a long time is dangerous.  Poisoned darts,
arrows, daggers, pit spikes, and trapped chests can all
potentially instakill you if you are not resistant.

Of course, you should avoid eating corpses that may be old
enough to give you food poisoning, but this is no more true
for bees than any other monster (except for lizards,
lichens, and I think maybe acid blobs).

